//! Caravan withdraw -- a phase still waiting may leave a run, and the same
//! three facts an arrival owed the plan are what make its leaving safe.
//!
//! `enlist.rye` carried a newcomer into a supervisor with dependents already
//! in flight, and named its own limit plainly: a run may take work while it
//! runs, and nothing may yet leave one. A phase queued by mistake, or made
//! pointless by a dependent that already came home, had no door out at all --
//! only a run carried to its end doing work nobody wanted, or a run torn
//! down and seated again from the top.
//!
//! **A withdrawal owes the plan the same three facts an arrival owed it,
//! read backwards, and that is the finding.** An arrival asks whether
//! anybody placed waits on its turn, whether its step is the next one that
//! turn has open, and whether a turn already standing agrees with it about
//! what it follows. A withdrawal asks the mirror of each: whether the phase
//! still waits, whether its step is the last one its turn holds, and whether
//! any phase in the record names its turn. One walk answers all three,
//! against the same record `enlist.rye` proved a run must keep whole.
//!
//! **The three facts are exactly what make a departure invisible downstream,
//! and that is why they are the right three.** A phase that still waits has
//! handed out no slot, no line, and no grant. A phase that is the last step
//! its turn holds has no sibling whose fence would fall open early. A phase
//! whose turn nobody names has no follower a supervisor could release by
//! mistake. Meet all three and every reading downstream -- `elder_waits`,
//! `sibling_waits`, `may_pass` -- answers exactly what it would have
//! answered had the phase never been written.
//!
//! **What a run must never do is release a follower whose predecessor never
//! ran.** A supervisor that asks only the plainest question -- does this
//! phase still wait -- lets turn 4 leave while turn 5 names it, and turn 5
//! then starts with `elder_waits` reading zero, satisfied by a turn that
//! never came home. Nothing reports it, which is what makes it worth
//! measuring: this module weighs the same phase under both readings and
//! shows the difference rather than asserting it.
//!
//! **A departure moves nothing.** In a run the record keeps its shape and
//! its length; the phase is marked gone where it stands, so every dependent
//! already started keeps the slot, the line, and the grants it was handed --
//! `enlist.rye`'s rule for a newcomer, read from the other side. On a plan
//! not yet running, a withdrawal closes the gap it leaves and every phase
//! that remains keeps the order its author wrote.
//!
//! **A withdrawal costs one walk of the record.** The departing phase is
//! weighed against each phase ever handed to the run exactly once, so the
//! whole cost is `max_withdraw_tests` against `max_seating_tests` to seat
//! the plan again -- the record's length against the queue's square, and
//! exactly what an arrival and an enlistment each cost.
//!
//! **The limit is named plainly.** A withdrawal reaches only work still
//! waiting: a dependent already running is never recalled, and a phase already
//! home is never unrun. Whether a run may *replace* a phase -- withdraw one
//! and enlist another in one act, so a plan may be corrected rather than
//! only grown and pruned -- belongs to the vision room until a witness binds
//! it.
//!
//! Usage:
//!   withdraw selftest                  Run the readings against each other
//!   withdraw                           Same as selftest
//!   withdraw dependent <domain> <plan> ... Run as a supervised dependent (internal)

const std = @import("std");
const assert = std.debug.assert;
const print = std.debug.print;
const system = @import("system.rye");
const capabilities = @import("capabilities.rye");
const roster = @import("roster.rye");
const read = @import("read.rye");
const boot = @import("boot.rye");
const exercise = @import("exercise.rye");
const carry = @import("carry.rye");
const notify = @import("notify.rye");
const roundtrip = @import("roundtrip.rye");
const cycle = @import("cycle.rye");
const gap = @import("gap.rye");
const cohort = @import("cohort.rye");
const intent = @import("intent.rye");
const mask = @import("mask.rye");
const precede = @import("precede.rye");
const arrive = @import("arrive.rye");
const enlist = @import("enlist.rye");

const caravan_withdraw_version = "20260819.205940";

// =========================================================================
// Bounds, carried from the rung below
// =========================================================================

/// The declaration this rung exercises, unchanged.
pub const declaration_path = enlist.declaration_path;

/// How many dependents one supervisor holds at once.
pub const max_in_flight: u32 = enlist.max_in_flight;

/// How many items one ordered queue carries.
pub const max_queue_len: u32 = enlist.max_queue_len;

/// How many still-waiting items past the head one turn may weigh.
pub const max_lookahead: u32 = enlist.max_lookahead;

/// A dependent's fixed argv, unchanged from the rungs below.
pub const fixed_argv_words: u32 = enlist.fixed_argv_words;

/// How many turns one queue may cut its work into.
pub const max_turns: u32 = enlist.max_turns;

/// How many pair tests one seating may ever spend.
pub const max_seating_tests: u32 = enlist.max_seating_tests;

/// How many tests one arrival at the door may ever spend.
pub const max_arrival_tests: u32 = enlist.max_arrival_tests;

/// How many tests one mid-run enlistment may ever spend.
pub const max_enlist_tests: u32 = enlist.max_enlist_tests;

/// How many tests one withdrawal may ever spend.
///
/// A withdrawal weighs the departing phase against the whole record exactly
/// once, gathering all three of its questions in that single walk, so
/// leaving costs precisely what joining costs. Stated here rather than left
/// for a reader to work out.
pub const max_withdraw_tests: u32 = max_enlist_tests;

/// How many phases one run may ever let go while it is under way.
///
/// A run can never release more work than it was handed, so the schedule is
/// bounded by the same number that bounds the record it prunes.
pub const max_withdrawals: u32 = max_queue_len;

comptime {
    // invariant: leaving costs exactly what joining a run under way costs
    assert(max_withdraw_tests == max_enlist_tests);
    // invariant: leaving costs exactly what arriving at the door costs
    assert(max_withdraw_tests == max_arrival_tests);
    // invariant: a withdrawal costs strictly less than seating the plan again
    assert(max_withdraw_tests < max_seating_tests);
    // invariant: a schedule never releases more work than one queue may hold
    assert(max_withdrawals <= max_queue_len);
}

/// Renders one outcome code as the words an operator reads.
pub fn outcome_name(code: u8) []const u8 {
    return enlist.outcome_name(code);
}

/// Why a queue may not take, or may not release, the work handed to it.
///
/// Three names of this rung's own, because a departure fails in three ways
/// an operator must tell apart: the phase was never in the record, it had
/// already left the waiting work, or the plan would not survive losing it.
pub const RunError = enlist.RunError || error{
    WithdrawalMissing,
    WithdrawalStarted,
    WithdrawalUnseated,
};

/// One queued item and the letters it declares, carried from `intent.rye`.
pub const Task = enlist.Task;

/// One phase, its turn, its step, and the two masks it carries, unchanged.
pub const Phase = enlist.Phase;

/// How deeply a reading looks at the queue's own authorship, unchanged.
pub const Reading = enlist.Reading;

/// Renders one reading as the words an operator reads.
pub fn reading_words(r: Reading) []const u8 {
    return enlist.reading_words(r);
}

/// What one run did, reported whole, unchanged from the rung below.
pub const Report = enlist.Report;

/// One newcomer and the moment the run offers it, unchanged.
pub const Enlistment = enlist.Enlistment;

/// The single bit that stands for one turn of a plan.
pub fn turn_bit(turn: u32) u32 {
    return enlist.turn_bit(turn);
}

/// Answers whether a newcomer may take the tail of a plan already seated.
pub fn arrival_admits(plan: []const Phase, newcomer: Phase) bool {
    return enlist.arrival_admits(plan, newcomer);
}

/// Answers whether the plan's written sequence keeps every name it carries.
pub fn plan_is_seated(plan: []const Phase) bool {
    return enlist.plan_is_seated(plan);
}

/// Answers whether two plans hold the same phases in the same places.
pub fn plans_match(a: []const Phase, b: []const Phase) bool {
    return enlist.plans_match(a, b);
}

/// Answers whether two phases must keep the order the queue wrote them in.
pub fn items_contend(sys: *const system.System, a: Phase, b: Phase, reading: Reading) bool {
    return enlist.items_contend(sys, a, b, reading);
}

/// Answers whether the head may enter beside the dependents running now.
pub fn admissible(
    sys: *const system.System,
    live: []const cohort.Running,
    head: Phase,
    reading: Reading,
) bool {
    return enlist.admissible(sys, live, head, reading);
}

// =========================================================================
// The departure -- one walk, and the mirror of the arrival's three facts
// =========================================================================

/// What one walk of a record learned about a phase asked to leave it.
///
/// Three questions share a walk because each of them is a fact about the
/// same phases: whether this phase stands here at all and still waits, how
/// far its own turn reaches, and whether anybody named that turn.
pub const Departing = struct {
    /// Where the phase stands, when it stands at all.
    at: u32 = 0,
    /// Some phase still present carries this turn and this step.
    found: bool = false,
    /// That phase has yet to be started.
    waiting: bool = false,
    /// The highest step of the departing turn still present in the record.
    reach: u32 = 0,
    /// Some other phase still present names the departing turn.
    named: bool = false,
};

/// Reads a record once and answers what a phase's departure would cost it.
///
/// The scan reads the masks the author declared rather than their closing,
/// for the reason `arrive.rye` gives: a turn reaches this turn transitively
/// only through some turn that names it outright, and any such turn either
/// stands in this record -- where the scan sees its own declaration -- or
/// stands outside it, where it holds nothing.
pub fn depart(
    plan: []const Phase,
    gone: []const bool,
    taken: []const bool,
    turn: u32,
    step: u32,
) Departing {
    // invariant: a departure always names a turn inside the bound
    assert(turn < max_turns);
    // invariant: a scan stays inside the queue one supervisor may hold
    assert(plan.len <= max_queue_len);
    // invariant: every phase in the record says whether it has left
    assert(gone.len == plan.len);
    // invariant: every phase in the record says whether it has started
    assert(taken.len == plan.len);
    var out: Departing = .{};
    var i: u32 = 0;
    while (i < plan.len) : (i += 1) {
        if (gone[i]) continue;
        if (plan[i].turn == turn) {
            if (plan[i].step > out.reach) out.reach = plan[i].step;
            if (plan[i].step == step and !out.found) {
                out.found = true;
                out.at = i;
                out.waiting = !taken[i];
            }
            continue;
        }
        if ((plan[i].follows_turns & turn_bit(turn)) != 0) out.named = true;
    }
    // invariant: the walk read the whole record, weighing every phase in it
    assert(i == plan.len);
    // invariant: a departure never stands outside the record it was read in
    assert(!out.found or out.at < plan.len);
    return out;
}

/// Answers why a phase may not leave a record, or that it may.
///
/// Three facts, and only three -- each the mirror of a fact an arrival owed
/// the same plan. The phase still waits, so it has handed out no slot, no
/// line, and no grant. Its step is the last one its turn holds, so no
/// sibling's fence falls open early. And no phase in the record names its
/// turn, so no follower is released by a predecessor that never ran.
pub fn withdrawal_refusal(
    plan: []const Phase,
    gone: []const bool,
    taken: []const bool,
    turn: u32,
    step: u32,
) ?RunError {
    // invariant: a record always carries work before anything leaves it
    assert(plan.len >= 1);
    // invariant: a withdrawal stays inside the queue one supervisor may hold
    assert(plan.len <= max_queue_len);
    const where = depart(plan, gone, taken, turn, step);
    if (!where.found) return error.WithdrawalMissing;
    if (!where.waiting) return error.WithdrawalStarted;
    if (step != where.reach) return error.WithdrawalUnseated;
    if (where.named) return error.WithdrawalUnseated;
    return null;
}

/// Answers whether a phase may leave a record at all.
pub fn withdrawal_admits(
    plan: []const Phase,
    gone: []const bool,
    taken: []const bool,
    turn: u32,
    step: u32,
) bool {
    return withdrawal_refusal(plan, gone, taken, turn, step) == null;
}

/// Writes a plan with one phase gone from it, or refuses.
///
/// The gap closes and nothing else moves: every phase that remains keeps the
/// name, the turn, the step, and the masks it was written with, in the order
/// its author wrote them. A plan grown by an arrival and then relieved of
/// that same phase is the plan the arrival was handed, phase for phase --
/// which is what makes a withdrawal the arrival's inverse rather than a
/// second reading of the same plan.
pub fn withdraw(plan: []const Phase, turn: u32, step: u32, out: []Phase) bool {
    // invariant: a withdrawal always has room for the plan it prunes
    assert(out.len + 1 == plan.len);
    // invariant: a withdrawal stays inside the queue one supervisor may hold
    assert(plan.len <= max_queue_len);
    const none: [max_queue_len]bool = @splat(false);
    if (!withdrawal_admits(plan, none[0..plan.len], none[0..plan.len], turn, step)) return false;
    var kept: u32 = 0;
    var i: u32 = 0;
    while (i < plan.len) : (i += 1) {
        if (plan[i].turn == turn and plan[i].step == step) continue;
        out[kept] = plan[i];
        kept += 1;
    }
    // invariant: the walk read the whole plan, weighing every phase in it
    assert(i == plan.len);
    // invariant: exactly the one phase asked for left the plan
    assert(kept == out.len);
    return true;
}

// =========================================================================
// The supervisor -- one record that may grow and shrink while it runs
// =========================================================================

/// One dependent already reaped, held until the whole record has drained.
const Finished = struct {
    domain: []const u8,
    verb: cycle.Verb,
    count: u32,
    expect: u8,
    code: u8,
};

/// Folds one reaped outcome into the report, or names the mismatch.
fn judge_outcome(done: Finished, report_out: *Report) RunError!void {
    // invariant: a judged dependent always names its domain
    assert(done.domain.len >= 1);
    // invariant: the report never counts more successes than dependents reaped
    assert(report_out.inner.run.succeeded <= report_out.inner.run.reaped);
    if (done.code != done.expect) {
        print("    {s}: expected {s}, heard {s}\n", .{
            done.domain, outcome_name(done.expect), outcome_name(done.code),
        });
        return error.OutcomeMismatch;
    }
    if (done.code == carry.Outcome.carried_ok) {
        report_out.inner.run.succeeded += 1;
        if (done.verb == .home) report_out.inner.run.homed += done.count;
    }
}

/// The queue's own bookkeeping for one run, over a record that may shrink.
///
/// `gone` is what makes this table different from the one below it: a phase
/// released while the run is under way keeps its place in the record and
/// stops being work, so every index already handed out stays exactly where
/// it was. `taken` and `gone` are kept apart on purpose -- one names work
/// that ran, the other names work that never will, and only the first is
/// ever judged at the end.
const Table = struct {
    live: [max_in_flight]cohort.Running = undefined,
    in_flight: u32 = 0,
    done: [max_queue_len]Finished = undefined,
    finished: u32 = 0,
    taken: [max_queue_len]bool = @splat(false),
    gone: [max_queue_len]bool = @splat(false),
    record: [max_queue_len]Phase = undefined,
    held: u32 = 0,
    released: u32 = 0,
    head: u32 = 0,
    left: u32 = 0,
};

/// The record as it stands right now.
fn standing(table: *const Table) []const Phase {
    // invariant: a record never outgrows the queue one supervisor may hold
    assert(table.held <= max_queue_len);
    return table.record[0..table.held];
}

/// Answers whether one phase of the record is still work waiting to run.
fn waits(table: *const Table, at: u32) bool {
    // invariant: a reading always names a phase inside the record
    assert(at < table.held);
    return !table.taken[at] and !table.gone[at];
}

/// Moves the head past every item already started or already released.
fn advance_head(table: *Table) void {
    // invariant: a head never walks past the record it reads
    assert(table.head <= table.held);
    while (table.head < table.held and !waits(table, table.head)) table.head += 1;
}

/// Answers whether a phase of a turn this pick's turn names still waits.
fn elder_waits(table: *const Table, pick: u32) bool {
    // invariant: a pick always names a phase inside the record
    assert(pick < table.held);
    const wanted = table.record[pick].follows_turns;
    if (wanted == 0) return false;
    var i: u32 = 0;
    while (i < table.held) : (i += 1) {
        if (i == pick) continue;
        if (!waits(table, i)) continue;
        if ((wanted & turn_bit(table.record[i].turn)) != 0) return true;
    }
    // invariant: the walk read the whole record, weighing every phase in it
    assert(i == table.held);
    return false;
}

/// Answers whether a sibling of this pick's own turn still waits behind it.
fn sibling_waits(table: *const Table, pick: u32, sibling_mask: u32) bool {
    // invariant: a pick always names a phase inside the record
    assert(pick < table.held);
    var i: u32 = 0;
    while (i < pick) : (i += 1) {
        if (!waits(table, i)) continue;
        if (table.record[i].turn != table.record[pick].turn) continue;
        if ((sibling_mask & mask.step_bit(table.record[i].step)) != 0) return true;
    }
    // invariant: the walk reached the pick, weighing every phase before it
    assert(i == pick);
    return false;
}

/// Answers whether a phase may be admitted ahead of the record's head.
fn may_pass(
    sys: *const system.System,
    table: *const Table,
    candidate: u32,
    reading: Reading,
) bool {
    // invariant: a pass always reaches forward, never at the head itself
    assert(candidate > table.head);
    // invariant: a candidate always stands inside the record
    assert(candidate < table.held);
    var i: u32 = table.head;
    while (i < candidate) : (i += 1) {
        if (!waits(table, i)) continue;
        if (items_contend(sys, table.record[i], table.record[candidate], reading)) return false;
    }
    // invariant: the walk reached the candidate, weighing every phase before it
    assert(i == candidate);
    return true;
}

/// Chooses one phase from behind a blocked head, or answers that none may go.
fn choose_pass(
    sys: *const system.System,
    table: *const Table,
    reading: Reading,
) ?u32 {
    // invariant: a pass is only ever sought while the head stands blocked
    assert(table.head < table.held);
    var looked: u32 = 0;
    var i: u32 = table.head + 1;
    while (i < table.held and looked < max_lookahead) : (i += 1) {
        if (!waits(table, i)) continue;
        looked += 1;
        if (!admissible(sys, table.live[0..table.in_flight], table.record[i], reading)) continue;
        if (!may_pass(sys, table, i, reading)) continue;
        return i;
    }
    // invariant: the look stayed inside the bound it was given
    assert(looked <= max_lookahead);
    return null;
}

/// Starts one phase, handing the line it declared and nothing more.
fn start_one(
    allocator: std.mem.Allocator,
    io: std.Io,
    self_path: []const u8,
    sys: *const system.System,
    caps: *const capabilities.CapabilityTable,
    phase: Phase,
    wake: gap.Wake,
) (RunError || cohort.RunError || boot.BootError)!cohort.Running {
    // invariant: a start always names the domain it starts
    assert(phase.task.item.domain.len >= 1);
    const narrowed = intent.narrow(caps, phase.task) orelse return error.UnknownDomain;
    const slot = narrowed.find_dependent(phase.task.item.domain) orelse return error.UnknownDomain;
    // invariant: a narrowed line stays inside what the document grants
    assert(boot.line_within(sys, slot));
    return cohort.spawn_one_within(
        allocator, io, self_path, sys, &narrowed, phase.task.item, wake, &.{},
    );
}

/// Admits as much of the record as the table, the isolation, and the reading
/// allow, and answers how many dependents it started.
fn fill_table(
    allocator: std.mem.Allocator,
    io: std.Io,
    self_path: []const u8,
    sys: *const system.System,
    caps: *const capabilities.CapabilityTable,
    wake: gap.Wake,
    reading: Reading,
    table: *Table,
    report_out: *Report,
) (RunError || cohort.RunError || boot.BootError)!u32 {
    var admitted: u32 = 0;
    while (table.in_flight < max_in_flight and table.left > 0) {
        advance_head(table);
        // invariant: work still waiting always leaves a head to weigh
        assert(table.head < table.held);

        var pick: u32 = table.head;
        if (!admissible(sys, table.live[0..table.in_flight], table.record[table.head], reading)) {
            pick = choose_pass(sys, table, reading) orelse break;
            report_out.inner.run.passes += 1;
            const reach = pick - table.head;
            if (reach > report_out.inner.run.pass_reach) report_out.inner.run.pass_reach = reach;
        }
        const chosen = table.record[pick];
        if (sibling_waits(table, pick, mask.prefix_mask(chosen.step))) {
            report_out.inner.out_of_turn += 1;
        }
        if (sibling_waits(table, pick, mask.prefix_mask(mask.fence_after(chosen.follows)))) {
            report_out.inner.out_of_fence += 1;
        }
        if (sibling_waits(table, pick, chosen.follows)) report_out.inner.out_of_mask += 1;
        if (elder_waits(table, pick)) report_out.out_of_precede += 1;

        table.live[table.in_flight] = try start_one(
            allocator, io, self_path, sys, caps, chosen, wake,
        );
        table.in_flight += 1;
        table.taken[pick] = true;
        table.left -= 1;
        admitted += 1;
        report_out.inner.run.admitted += 1;
    }
    // invariant: a fill never overruns the table it fills
    assert(table.in_flight <= max_in_flight);
    // invariant: a preceded reading never runs a phase past a turn its turn named
    assert(reading != .preceded or report_out.out_of_precede == 0);
    return admitted;
}

/// Waits on the eldest dependent, records what it answered, and closes the table
/// over the slot it leaves.
fn reap_oldest(io: std.Io, table: *Table, report_out: *Report) cohort.RunError!void {
    // invariant: a reaping always has a dependent to wait on
    assert(table.in_flight >= 1);
    // invariant: a reaping never overruns the record it is kept in
    assert(table.finished < max_queue_len);
    const code = try cohort.reap_one(io, &table.live[0]);
    table.done[table.finished] = .{
        .domain = table.live[0].domain,
        .verb = table.live[0].verb,
        .count = table.live[0].count,
        .expect = table.live[0].expect,
        .code = code,
    };
    table.finished += 1;
    table.in_flight -= 1;
    report_out.inner.run.reaped += 1;
    report_out.inner.run.turns += 1;

    var s: u32 = 0;
    while (s < table.in_flight) : (s += 1) table.live[s] = table.live[s + 1];
    // invariant: the table closed over the reaped dependent, none lost
    assert(s == table.in_flight);
}

// =========================================================================
// The withdrawal -- one act the record's own memory makes safe
// =========================================================================

/// One phase asked to leave, and the moment the run releases it.
///
/// `after` counts dependents reaped, so a schedule reads as plainly as the run
/// it describes: this phase leaves once that many dependents have come home.
/// A phase is named by its turn and its step, the way its author wrote it,
/// rather than by an index the record might have moved.
pub const Withdrawal = struct {
    after: u32,
    turn: u32,
    step: u32,
};

/// Releases one waiting phase from a running record, or names why it stays.
///
/// One walk and no more, over the whole record rather than the work still
/// waiting -- the same record `enlist.rye` proved a run must keep, read for
/// the opposite act. Nothing already placed moves, so the slots, lines, and
/// grants of every dependent in flight stand exactly as they were handed out.
fn withdraw_one(table: *Table, turn: u32, step: u32) RunError!void {
    // invariant: a run always carries work before anything leaves it
    assert(table.held >= 1);
    const gone = table.gone[0..table.held];
    const taken = table.taken[0..table.held];
    if (withdrawal_refusal(standing(table), gone, taken, turn, step)) |why| return why;
    const where = depart(standing(table), gone, taken, turn, step);
    // invariant: an admitted departure always found the phase it releases
    assert(where.found);
    // invariant: a released phase was work still waiting a moment ago
    assert(waits(table, where.at));
    table.gone[where.at] = true;
    table.released += 1;
    table.left -= 1;
    // invariant: the record kept its length, so no index handed out moved
    assert(table.held <= max_queue_len);
    // invariant: work still waiting never outruns the record that holds it
    assert(table.left <= table.held);
}

/// Runs a record that may grow and shrink while it runs, taking each
/// newcomer and releasing each departure at the moment its schedule names.
///
/// The supervisor is the one every rung in this arc keeps -- fill the table,
/// reap the eldest, judge at the end -- with exactly two acts added after
/// each reaping: every newcomer whose moment has come is weighed against the
/// record as it now stands, and every departure whose moment has come is
/// weighed against that same record. A refusal arrives before the next dependent
/// starts and leaves the run it interrupted exactly as it found it.
pub fn run_with_changes(
    allocator: std.mem.Allocator,
    io: std.Io,
    self_path: []const u8,
    sys: *const system.System,
    base: []const Phase,
    schedule: []const Enlistment,
    departures: []const Withdrawal,
    wake: gap.Wake,
    reading: Reading,
    report_out: *Report,
) (roster.RosterError || exercise.ProvisionError || notify.BellError || RunError || cohort.RunError || boot.BootError)!void {
    // invariant: a run always knows what program to spawn
    assert(self_path.len >= 1);
    // invariant: a run always reports into a fresh report
    assert(report_out.inner.run.admitted == 0);
    if (base.len == 0) return error.EmptyQueue;
    if (base.len + schedule.len > max_queue_len) return error.QueueFull;
    if (schedule.len > enlist.max_enlistments) return error.QueueFull;
    if (departures.len > max_withdrawals) return error.QueueFull;
    if (!precede.plan_is_ordered(base)) return error.OrderStalled;
    if (!plan_is_seated(base)) return error.PlanUnseated;

    var table: Table = .{};
    precede.close(base, table.record[0..base.len]);
    table.held = @intCast(base.len);
    table.left = table.held;
    // invariant: a closed record closes to itself, so the door's work is done
    assert(precede.plan_is_closed(standing(&table)));

    const provisioned = try exercise.provision(io, sys);
    // invariant: every declared region has a backing store before any dependent runs
    assert(provisioned == sys.map.region_count);
    report_out.inner.run.bells = try roundtrip.provision_directed(io, sys);
    const caps = try roster.from_system(sys);
    // invariant: the derived table enforces exactly what the document permits
    assert(roster.agrees(sys, &caps));
    report_out.inner.run.queued = table.held;

    var offered: u32 = 0;
    var released: u32 = 0;
    while (table.left > 0 or table.in_flight > 0) {
        const admitted_now = try fill_table(
            allocator, io, self_path, sys, &caps, wake, reading, &table, report_out,
        );
        if (table.in_flight > report_out.inner.run.peak_in_flight) {
            report_out.inner.run.peak_in_flight = table.in_flight;
        }

        if (table.left > 0) {
            const free = max_in_flight - table.in_flight;
            report_out.inner.run.slots_unspent += free;
            if (admitted_now == 0 and free > 0) report_out.inner.run.idle_turns += 1;
        }

        // With an empty table nothing conflicts, so a stall here would mean
        // the record named a domain the document does not.
        if (table.in_flight == 0) return error.OrderStalled;
        try reap_oldest(io, &table, report_out);

        while (offered < schedule.len and schedule[offered].after <= report_out.inner.run.reaped) {
            try enlist_one(&table, schedule[offered].phase);
            report_out.inner.run.queued += 1;
            offered += 1;
        }
        while (released < departures.len and departures[released].after <= report_out.inner.run.reaped) {
            try withdraw_one(&table, departures[released].turn, departures[released].step);
            released += 1;
        }
    }
    // invariant: every newcomer the schedule named was offered, none skipped
    assert(offered == schedule.len);
    // invariant: every departure the schedule named was released, none skipped
    assert(released == departures.len);
    // invariant: the whole record was admitted or released, and every dependent reaped
    assert(table.left == 0);
    assert(table.in_flight == 0);
    assert(report_out.inner.run.reaped == report_out.inner.run.admitted);
    assert(table.finished + table.released == table.held);

    var j: u32 = 0;
    while (j < table.finished) : (j += 1) try judge_outcome(table.done[j], report_out);
    // invariant: every reaped dependent was judged, none skipped
    assert(j == table.finished);
}

/// Takes one newcomer into a running record, or names why it may not join.
///
/// Carried whole from `enlist.rye`, reading the record as this rung keeps
/// it: a newcomer lands at the tail, and every phase already placed -- run,
/// waiting, or released -- keeps exactly where it stands.
fn enlist_one(table: *Table, newcomer: Phase) RunError!void {
    // invariant: a run always carries work before anything joins it
    assert(table.held >= 1);
    if (table.held == max_queue_len) return error.QueueFull;
    if (!arrival_admits(standing(table), newcomer)) return error.ArrivalUnseated;
    table.record[table.held] = newcomer;
    table.taken[table.held] = false;
    table.gone[table.held] = false;
    table.held += 1;
    table.left += 1;
    // invariant: the record grew by exactly the one phase offered
    assert(table.held <= max_queue_len);
    // invariant: work still waiting never outruns the record that holds it
    assert(table.left <= table.held);
}

// =========================================================================
// The lap -- one plan, handed whole and handed while it shrinks
// =========================================================================

/// The lap every rung in this arc runs, written in the order its names imply.
///
/// One busy domain makes the room: `client_a` opens with a place and three
/// more turns of the same domain queue behind it, so the head stands blocked
/// and a pass is the only way forward. Turn 4 has `client_b` place into
/// `ask_b` and names turn 3; turn 5 has `client_c` peek the published `menu`
/// and names turn 4 alone; turn 6 names nothing at all.
const written_queue = [_]Phase{
    .{ .turn = 0, .step = 0, .follows = 0, .follows_turns = 0, .task = .{ .effects = "w", .item = .{ .domain = "client_a", .verb = .place, .hops = "ask_a", .peers = "serial_virt", .count = 1, .expect = carry.Outcome.carried_ok } } },
    .{ .turn = 1, .step = 0, .follows = 0, .follows_turns = 0, .task = .{ .effects = "r", .item = .{ .domain = "client_a", .verb = .peek, .hops = "menu", .peers = "serial_virt", .count = 0, .expect = carry.Outcome.bytes_differed } } },
    .{ .turn = 2, .step = 0, .follows = 0, .follows_turns = 0, .task = .{ .effects = "r", .item = .{ .domain = "client_a", .verb = .peek, .hops = "back_a", .peers = "serial_virt", .count = 0, .expect = carry.Outcome.bytes_differed } } },
    .{ .turn = 3, .step = 0, .follows = 0, .follows_turns = 0, .task = .{ .effects = "r", .item = .{ .domain = "client_a", .verb = .peek, .hops = "taken_a", .peers = "serial_virt", .count = 0, .expect = carry.Outcome.bytes_differed } } },
    .{ .turn = 4, .step = 0, .follows = 0, .follows_turns = 8, .task = .{ .effects = "w", .item = .{ .domain = "client_b", .verb = .place, .hops = "ask_b", .peers = "serial_virt", .count = 1, .expect = carry.Outcome.carried_ok } } },
    .{ .turn = 5, .step = 0, .follows = 0, .follows_turns = 16, .task = .{ .effects = "r", .item = .{ .domain = "client_c", .verb = .peek, .hops = "menu", .peers = "serial_virt", .count = 0, .expect = carry.Outcome.bytes_differed } } },
    .{ .turn = 6, .step = 0, .follows = 0, .follows_turns = 0, .task = .{ .effects = "r", .item = .{ .domain = "client_b", .verb = .peek, .hops = "back_b", .peers = "serial_virt", .count = 0, .expect = carry.Outcome.bytes_differed } } },
};

/// The tail of that lap, released one phase at a time while the run is under
/// way rather than pruned before the door.
///
/// Turns 1 and 2 leave once the opening dependent has come home, with dependents
/// still in flight and their slots already granted -- which is the whole
/// point of the rung. Both are `client_a` peeks queued behind the busy head,
/// so neither can have started while turn 0 held that domain; nobody names
/// either turn; and each is the only step its turn holds. The plan survives
/// losing them, and the metal is what says so: an earlier draft of this
/// schedule reached for turns 5 and 6, which the passes had already started,
/// and the run refused with `WithdrawalStarted` rather than pretending.
const late_departures = [_]Withdrawal{
    .{ .after = 1, .turn = 2, .step = 0 },
    .{ .after = 1, .turn = 1, .step = 0 },
};

/// The phase a shy run would release, and the follower it would strand.
///
/// Turn 4 is named by turn 5, which follows it. Against the whole record the
/// answer is plain: releasing turn 4 would leave turn 5 waiting on a turn
/// that never comes home, so the departure is refused by name. A supervisor
/// asking only whether turn 4 still waits would let it go, and turn 5 would
/// then start with `elder_waits` reading zero -- satisfied by a predecessor
/// that never ran, with nothing anywhere to report it.
const named_turn: u32 = 4;

/// The follower that shy reading would release.
const following_turn: u32 = 5;

// =========================================================================
// Self-test
// =========================================================================

/// Loads one declaration, or names why it could not be read.
fn load_one(io: std.Io, path: []const u8, buf: []u8) ?system.System {
    const parsed = read.load(io, path, buf) catch |err| {
        print("  RED: {s} refused: {s}\n", .{ path, @errorName(err) });
        return null;
    };
    if (parsed.verify() != .whole) {
        print("  RED: {s} did not read whole\n", .{path});
        return null;
    }
    return parsed;
}

/// The withdrawal read straight, before any supervisor spends it.
///
/// The happy zone of this rung: a table is built by hand, phases are marked
/// started, and every question is a pure fold over the record -- answered
/// instantly, with no dependent started and no store touched.
pub fn check_withdrawal() u8 {
    var table: Table = .{};
    var i: u32 = 0;
    while (i < written_queue.len) : (i += 1) table.record[i] = written_queue[i];
    table.held = i;
    table.left = table.held;
    // invariant: the hand-built record holds every phase it was given
    assert(table.held == written_queue.len);

    // A phase nobody names, standing last in its own turn, leaves a running
    // record exactly as it would leave a plan, and the record keeps its
    // length so no index handed out ever moves.
    withdraw_one(&table, 6, 0) catch {
        print("  RED: a phase nobody waits on was refused its leave\n", .{});
        return 1;
    };
    if (table.held != written_queue.len) {
        print("  RED: a departure moved the record, leaving {d} places\n", .{table.held});
        return 1;
    }

    // The three refusals, each named for the fact it protects.
    const named = withdraw_one(&table, named_turn, 0);
    if (named) |_| {
        print("  RED: a turn its follower names was released anyway\n", .{});
        return 1;
    } else |err| {
        if (err != error.WithdrawalUnseated) {
            print("  RED: the record refused for the wrong reason: {s}\n", .{@errorName(err)});
            return 1;
        }
    }
    const absent = withdraw_one(&table, 6, 0);
    if (absent) |_| {
        print("  RED: a phase already released left the record a second time\n", .{});
        return 1;
    } else |err| {
        if (err != error.WithdrawalMissing) {
            print("  RED: a released phase refused for the wrong reason: {s}\n", .{@errorName(err)});
            return 1;
        }
    }
    table.taken[0] = true;
    table.left -= 1;
    const started = withdraw_one(&table, 0, 0);
    if (started) |_| {
        print("  RED: a phase already started was recalled\n", .{});
        return 1;
    } else |err| {
        if (err != error.WithdrawalStarted) {
            print("  RED: a started phase refused for the wrong reason: {s}\n", .{@errorName(err)});
            return 1;
        }
    }

    // What the shy reading costs, measured rather than asserted: release the
    // named turn on the one question a supervisor would think to ask, and
    // its follower's own wait reads satisfied by a turn that never ran.
    var shy: Table = .{};
    var k: u32 = 0;
    while (k < written_queue.len) : (k += 1) shy.record[k] = written_queue[k];
    shy.held = k;
    shy.left = shy.held;
    const at_named = index_of(&shy, named_turn) orelse {
        print("  RED: the record lost the turn this reading weighs\n", .{});
        return 1;
    };
    const at_follower = index_of(&shy, following_turn) orelse {
        print("  RED: the record lost the follower this reading weighs\n", .{});
        return 1;
    };
    if (!elder_waits(&shy, at_follower)) {
        print("  RED: the follower never waited on the turn it names\n", .{});
        return 1;
    }
    shy.gone[at_named] = true;
    shy.left -= 1;
    if (elder_waits(&shy, at_follower)) {
        print("  RED: the shy reading kept the wait, so nothing was shown\n", .{});
        return 1;
    }

    print("  a turn its follower names is refused its leave against a record of {d}\n", .{
        table.held,
    });
    print("  the shy reading lets it go, and turn {d} then waits on nobody\n", .{following_turn});
    print("  a withdrawal costs at most {d} tests, against {d} to seat the plan again\n", .{
        max_withdraw_tests, max_seating_tests,
    });
    return 0;
}

/// Answers where one turn's only step stands in a record.
fn index_of(table: *const Table, turn: u32) ?u32 {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    while (i < table.held) : (i += 1) {
        if (table.record[i].turn == turn) return i;
    }
    // invariant: the walk read the whole record, weighing every phase in it
    assert(i == table.held);
    return null;
}

/// The inverse test: an arrival relieved of its own phase is the plan it
/// was handed, phase for phase.
///
/// This arc's standing generalization test, one tier further out. An empty
/// turn mask was the sibling mask, a full sibling mask was the fence, a
/// seated plan arranged to itself, and a plan grown one arrival at a time
/// was the plan its author wrote. Here a plan grown by an arrival and then
/// relieved of that arrival is the plan again, exactly.
pub fn check_inverse() u8 {
    var grown: [max_queue_len]Phase = undefined;
    var pruned: [max_queue_len]Phase = undefined;
    const base = written_queue[0..6];
    if (!arrive.arrive(base, written_queue[6], grown[0 .. base.len + 1])) {
        print("  RED: a newcomer nobody waits on was refused the tail\n", .{});
        return 1;
    }
    if (!withdraw(grown[0 .. base.len + 1], 6, 0, pruned[0..base.len])) {
        print("  RED: the plan refused to let go of the phase it just took\n", .{});
        return 1;
    }
    if (!plans_match(pruned[0..base.len], base)) {
        print("  RED: a plan relieved of its arrival is not the plan it was\n", .{});
        return 1;
    }
    if (!plan_is_seated(pruned[0..base.len])) {
        print("  RED: a pruned plan no longer seats itself\n", .{});
        return 1;
    }
    print("  a plan relieved of its own arrival is that plan, all {d} phases\n", .{base.len});
    return 0;
}

/// Runs one queue whole and answers its report.
fn run_one(
    allocator: std.mem.Allocator,
    io: std.Io,
    self_path: []const u8,
    sys: *const system.System,
    plan: []const Phase,
    reading: Reading,
    report_out: *Report,
) bool {
    run_with_changes(
        allocator, io, self_path, sys, plan, &.{}, &.{}, .when_moved, reading, report_out,
    ) catch |err| {
        print("  RED: a queue did not survive its run: {s}\n", .{@errorName(err)});
        return false;
    };
    return true;
}

/// Runs one queue that shrinks while it runs and answers its report.
fn run_shrinking(
    allocator: std.mem.Allocator,
    io: std.Io,
    self_path: []const u8,
    sys: *const system.System,
    base: []const Phase,
    departures: []const Withdrawal,
    reading: Reading,
    report_out: *Report,
) bool {
    run_with_changes(
        allocator, io, self_path, sys, base, &.{}, departures, .when_moved, reading, report_out,
    ) catch |err| {
        print("  RED: a shrinking queue did not survive its run: {s}\n", .{@errorName(err)});
        return false;
    };
    return true;
}

/// The withdrawal lap: one plan run twice, handed whole and pruned as it runs.
pub fn check_order(allocator: std.mem.Allocator, io: std.Io, self_path: []const u8) u8 {
    var buf: [read.read_buffer_bytes]u8 = undefined;
    const sys = load_one(io, declaration_path, &buf) orelse return 1;

    var whole: Report = .{};
    if (!run_one(allocator, io, self_path, &sys, &written_queue, .preceded, &whole)) return 1;
    var shrinking: Report = .{};
    if (!run_shrinking(
        allocator, io, self_path, &sys, &written_queue, &late_departures, .preceded, &shrinking,
    )) return 1;

    print("  breaks a named turn: {d} handed whole, {d} pruned while running\n", .{
        whole.out_of_precede, shrinking.out_of_precede,
    });
    print("  dependents: {d} handed whole, {d} pruned while running\n", .{
        whole.inner.run.reaped, shrinking.inner.run.reaped,
    });
    print("  {d} phases left a run already under way\n", .{late_departures.len});

    if (shrinking.out_of_precede != 0) {
        print("  RED: the shrinking run broke {d} turn orders its author named\n", .{
            shrinking.out_of_precede,
        });
        return 1;
    }
    const expected = whole.inner.run.reaped - late_departures.len;
    if (shrinking.inner.run.reaped != expected) {
        print("  RED: the shrinking queue reaped {d} dependents against {d} expected\n", .{
            shrinking.inner.run.reaped, expected,
        });
        return 1;
    }
    // invariant: a run reaps exactly the dependents it admitted, never more
    assert(shrinking.inner.run.reaped == shrinking.inner.run.admitted);
    // invariant: releasing work never runs work the whole hand did not
    assert(shrinking.inner.run.succeeded <= whole.inner.run.succeeded);

    return 0;
}

fn run_self_test(allocator: std.mem.Allocator, io: std.Io, self_path: []const u8) u8 {
    print("Caravan withdraw {s} -- self-test\n", .{caravan_withdraw_version});
    const reading = check_withdrawal();
    if (reading != 0) return reading;
    const inverse = check_inverse();
    if (inverse != 0) return inverse;
    const order = check_order(allocator, io, self_path);
    if (order != 0) return order;
    print("  GREEN: a phase still waiting may leave a run, on the mirror of the three facts an arrival owed\n", .{});
    return 0;
}

pub fn main(init: std.process.Init) !u8 {
    const allocator = init.arena.allocator();
    const args = try init.minimal.args.toSlice(allocator);
    const io = init.io;
    // invariant: a program always knows its own path
    assert(args.len >= 1);
    const self_path = args[0];

    if (args.len >= fixed_argv_words and std.mem.eql(u8, args[1], "dependent")) {
        return cohort.run_dependent(io, args);
    }
    if (args.len >= 2 and std.mem.eql(u8, args[1], "selftest")) {
        return run_self_test(allocator, io, self_path);
    }
    if (args.len >= 2) return 1;
    return run_self_test(allocator, io, self_path);
}
